invariant: INV-17
file: sha512.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: a host object's sha384_of returns without wiping the context it
  hashed in, so its dead frame keeps the state after the last block and
  the end of the input. HMAC-SHA-384 hashes a key longer than a block
  through this call, and the bytes left are the key's last ones and the
  value HMAC then uses as its key; keysched.c's exporter hashes its
  caller's context through it. The digest is still right, so no vector
  sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test paints the stack, makes one sha384_of call
  on sha512.c's first arm, and requires no word the call computed in the
  bytes it wrote.

--- old
    sha384_final(&s, out);
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    sha384_final(&s, out);
